cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BRPT in scientific work, please cite the software release used in your computations."
title: "BRPT: cubic Frobenius probable-primality test"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Righi
    given-names: Marco
  - family-names: Baldi
    given-names: Michele
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and validation suite for the BRPT cubic Frobenius
  probable-primality test. The repository contains the primality-test engine,
  reproducible test campaigns for external datasets, ring scans, exact-prime
  validation, and diagnostic plotting tools.
keywords:
  - primality testing
  - probable prime
  - Frobenius test
  - cubic polynomial
  - Carmichael numbers
  - pseudoprimes
  - computational number theory
